# The build context is the repository root, because the images need both the
# application source and the files under docker/. Everything that is not part of
# an image is excluded — not only for build speed, but because a stale local
# artefact silently baked into an image is a class of bug that only shows up in
# production. The framework's cached package manifest is exactly that: built from
# the development dependency set, it would name a provider the production image
# does not contain.

.git
.github
.claude
docs
load
sdk
sink

**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example

backend/vendor
backend/bootstrap/cache/*.php
backend/storage/logs/*.log
backend/storage/framework/cache/data/*
backend/storage/framework/sessions/*
backend/storage/framework/views/*.php
backend/.phpunit.cache
backend/.phpunit.result.cache

frontend/node_modules
frontend/.next
frontend/out

*.md
!README.md
